'''Jon Favreau''' (born [[October 19]], [[1960s#1966|1966]]) is an [[Wikipedia:American|American]] actor, director, and screenwriter who provided the voice of the [[Mandalorian]] [[Pre Vizsla]] in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', the [[Ardennian]] pilot [[Rio Durant]] in ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', and the Mandalorian [[Paz Vizsla]] in ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''.

==Biography==
Jon Favreau was born on [[October 19]], [[1960s#1966|1966]]<ref name="ThisWeek22" /> in [[Wikipedia:Flushing|Flushing]], [[Wikipedia:New York|New York]].<ref name="FavreauBirth" />

Before the release of ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', director [[Ron Howard]] revealed that Favreau would have a voice role in the film, as a "very cool & important" [[alien]] character.<ref name="Jon Favreau">{{Twitter|RealRonHoward|status/963873491358441474|[[Ron Howard]]|quote=Wondering why we r all together? @Jon_Favreau is voicing a very cool & important alien character for #HanSolo Flattered & fortunate I could pull him away from his #LionKing directing duties|archivedate=20191027100337}}</ref> Favreau later revealed an image of his character on Twitter.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|Jon_Favreau|status/964516975899697153|Jon Favreau|quote=#Solo #StarWars|archivedate=20190807183214}}</ref>

[[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] wanted something as big as the films for the release of their streaming service [[Disney+]], so [[Lucasfilm]] President [[Kathleen Kennedy]] first turned to Favreau who said he had an idea and that he would commit to ''[[Star Wars]]''. After their meeting at Kennedy's office, Favreau started writing without a contract. When he was officially hired, he had written the first four episodes about a [[Mandalorian]]. Kennedy arranged a meeting between Favreau and [[Dave Filoni]] in [[Wikipedia:Los Angeles|Los Angeles]] in which they exchanged ideas and drawings for a Mandalorian show. Favreau combined his concept of a lone gunslinger with Filoni's knowledge of Mandalorian history. Favreau's idea was [[Din Grogu|the Child]], which the two spent time debating. Favreau and the crew wanted the Child to look goofy and ugly instead of looking too cute. [[Christian Alzmann]]'s drawing of the Child was the first one that finally clicked. Favreau recruited [[Pedro Pascal]] to play the Mandalorian, whose name was later revealed to be [[Din Djarin]].<ref name="Rebellion televised">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2022/05/star-wars-cover-the-rebellion-will-be-televised|text=''Star Wars:'' The Rebellion Will Be Televised|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2022-05-17|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20220517110251}}</ref>

On [[March 8]], [[2018]], it was revealed that Favreau would write and executive produce the upcoming live-action ''Star Wars'' television series,<ref name="Favreau">{{SW|url=news/jon-favreau-to-executive-produce-write-live-action-star-wars-series|text=Jon Favreau to Executive Produce and Write Live-Action ''Star Wars'' Series}}</ref> ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''.<ref name="The Mandalorian FB">{{Facebook|username=jonfavreau|url=jonfavreau/photos/a.437300899719695/1871991379583966|name=Jon Favreau|date=October 3, 2018|quote=#StarWars #TheMandalorian|archivefile=File:Jon_Favreau_The_Mandalorian.png|archivedate=20140730005136}}</ref> On [[May 10]], 2018, in an interview with [[Anthony Carboni]] on the premiere of ''Solo: A Star Wars Story'', Favreau revealed that he was halfway done with writing a season of the series.<ref name="Solo premiere">{{SWYouTube|VfdTeJdu1xw|Live From the Red Carpet of ''Solo: A Star Wars -2022 Story''!}}</ref> When Favreau and<ref name="Tells all">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2020/11/rosario-dawson-dave-filoni-mandalorian-ahsoka-tano-grogu|text=Star Wars The Mandalorian: Rosario Dawson Tells All About Ahsoka Tano|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2020-11-30|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20201207031817}}</ref> executive producer<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> Dave Filoni started working together, Filoni would bring up [[Ahsoka Tano]] and say that [[Rosario Dawson]] was at the top of his lost for the role. Favreau revealed that he knew the actress, which helped the casting process.<ref name="Tells all" /> Favreau and Filoni did not want to bring Tano into the show in the [[The Mandalorian Season One|first season]].<ref name="Best of Jedi">{{SW|url=news/rosario-dawson-ahsoka-tano-interview|text=The Best of the Jedi: Rosario Dawson on Bringing Ahsoka Tano to Live-Action and ''The Mandalorian''}}</ref> During early production of Season One, Favreau told Filoni that the Child's name would be Grogu. They knew they wanted Tano in [[The Mandalorian Season Two|Season Two's]] story, so they started visualizing Dawson in the role, and art of her playing Tano was created. Near the release of the first season, Dawson got a [[Wikipedia:FaceTime|FaceTime]] call from Favreau and Filoni, and they showed her visuals and concept from their plans for Season Two, including art of her as Tano. They asked Dawson if she wanted to play Tano and she agreed.<ref name="Tells all" />

During the The Walt Disney Company's Investor Day event on [[December 10]], [[2020]], it was revealed that Favreau, along with Filoni, would executive produce two television series that would connect to ''The Mandalorian''&ndash;''[[Rangers of the New Republic]]'' and ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]''.<ref name="Dec 10">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}}</ref> Favreau created the ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'' television series and worked as a writer and executive producer.<ref name="Stranger">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref> He created the [[Mods]] and wanted them to have a retro punk aesthetic.<ref name="Captures spirit">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2022/artisans/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-costumes-shawna-trpcic-star-wars-1235170729|text=How 'The Book of Boba Fett' Costume Designer Shawna Trpcic Captures the Spirit of the Original 'Star Wars' Trilogy|author=Chapman, Wilson|date=2022-02-03|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20220203182220}}</ref>

When Filoni was writing the episodes for ''Ahsoka'', Favreau enhanced his writing by pointing out things from the perspective of someone not deep in animation and Ahsoka Tano's history.<ref name="Ahsoka for life">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2022/05/rosario-dawson-ahsoka-tano-star-wars-series|text=''Star Wars'': Rosario Dawson Aims To Play Ahsoka Tano For Life|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2022-05-20|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20220520134642}}</ref> After actress [[Natasha Liu Bordizzo]] sent a self-tape, Favreau tried to make the casting process as seamless as possible. Months later, Bordizzo met Favreau and Filoni, and the former explained what he did. After Bordizzo was cast as the Mandalorian [[Sabine Wren]]<ref name="Day Shift">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/day-shift-natasha-liu-bordizzo-star-wars-sabine-wren-1235202889|text='Day Shift' Star Natasha Liu Bordizzo Is Living Her 'Star Wars' Dream as Sabine Wren|author=Davids, Brian|date=2022-08-20|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|archivedate=20221016144800}}</ref> in [[2021]],<ref name="Rosario Natasha SWCA">{{SWYouTube|8RZiIf_oEAc|Rosario Dawson and Natasha Liu Bordizzo takes the stage at SWCA 2022 &#124; Star Wars Celebration Live!}}</ref> Favreau and Filoni told the actress it would be great if she watched ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', but they said the live-action version would always be a new thing that finds its own truth.<ref name="Day Shift" /> ''Ahsoka'' started production on [[May 9]], [[2022]].<ref name="Ahsoka begins">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-begins-production|text=''Ahsoka'', the Upcoming Disney+ Original Series, Begins Production}}</ref> At Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase at [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|Celebration Anaheim]], [[2022]], Favreau and Filoni played a video message from Rosario Dawson in her full costume from the show's set. Favreau then told the audience they could see costumes and props from ''The Mandalorian'' in a special exhibit.<ref name="20 Highlights">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-20-highlights-from-lucasfilms-studio-showcase|text=SWCA 2022: 20 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> At the Mando+ panel, Favreau and Filoni showed the first footage from ''Ahsoka'' and introduced Bordizzo as Wren in the series.<ref name="MandoPlus">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-mando-plus-panel|text=SWCA 2022: Sabine Wren Joins the Cast of ''Ahsoka'' and 6 Other Favorite Moments from the Mando+ Panel}}</ref>

